{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794445496,"nonce":"3/vfohxUVLB7/jWSBRFaHO+oaFE=","title":"Two full paints of the same spring-driven scene differ","message":"In the animation-path harness, replaying one scripted spring scene twice in the same process gives two sets of frames that differ: 540 to 700 px at a two-level threshold, up to about 13 levels, along the edges of the moving box. The patched path replayed twice is identical to itself, so the full paint is the unstable one; the first run in a process differs from the ones after it.\n\nThe stepping is fixed (`tick_by`, `FrameClock::begin_frame_at`), so the values should not move. Suspects: the process-wide scheduler `Headless` shares between sessions, or a promoted layer's texture sampled at a fractional position. Not found.\n\nThe harness compares at 24 levels because of it. A real divergence is over 200.","files":null}]}